    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0930" n="794" xml:id="pg794"/>

                <head>No. 564.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Sir L. S. Sackville
                            West</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 21,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: By your note of the 20th instant, which I
                    had the honor to receive this morning, you refer to your note of the 19th,
                    touching the second meeting of the sugar conference at London, April 5; and
                    further express the request of the Marquis of Salisbury that the documents
                    referred to in the protocol of 19th December, 1887, may be communicated to Her
                    Majesty’s Government as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>Supplementing my reply of this date to your note of the 19th instant, I have to
                    say touching the provision of the protocol to which you refer—to the effect that
                    governments contemplating adhesion to the proposed convention should give notice
                    of such intention before March 1, communicating at the same time the system of
                    taxation they may propose for carrying out its provisions, and the method and
                    extent of the employment of saccharometric tests—that as this Government is
                    unprepared at present to accept the convention itself, it is necessarily
                    unprepared to give the detailed statements suggested, especially as the subject
                    is one of pending legislation affecting the revenue.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
